{
  "case": "15-derived-ids",
  "description": "Rule-created agents are named from the REDEX (rule + the two parent ids + an ordinal within the rewrite), not from a running counter, so the ids a reduction produces are a property of the net rather than of the schedule. This net has two independent redexes, so different schedules genuinely fire in different orders; `pin_ids` + `schedules` therefore assert the strong property directly: 16 randomized orders must agree on the literal agent names, not merely on the id-independent canonical form. Peers merging by reduction depend on this — confluence alone gives the same normal form only up to renaming, which is the same shape but not the same bytes. An implementation that mints ids sequentially, randomly, or from a clock passes every other case in this suite and fails this one.",
